# S2c: one of THREE runs (S2a..S2c), each after its own all-four reset, of the AUDITS-OFF hang shapes on c2-packed-tp4-best-strace-tpub: the combined best (audits off, the pinned sampler
# recorded in the verify trace, the tail caps, the fused commit, the quad) plus the traced carry copies. This is the allocation-order gate of docs/tp4-tpub.md: the request engine now captures
# two more traces (carry save and restore) in its own build, after its verify and commit traces, and production trace shape is safe only by layout. THREE CONSECUTIVE COMPLETIONS are the
# evidence (the best-strace window needs five on the base; these three are on top of a base that already passed them); one stall restarts the count, stops the window and leaves the cards hung
# until the hand-back reset. Read: every test completes, no stall-watch stack dump, the engaged line once per request engine and no declined line, '[PINDIAG] four-card engine programs='
# deltas small after the captures, no late prefill program.
# STOP on a stall, a hang or a decline.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1 to 3 min, build 10 to 20 min on a warm cache, the shapes 15 to 20 min: 40 min per run.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/tpub window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/tpub and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image a build-only job (C2_ACTIONS=build, no card opened) builds from this branch while
# production serves; a later commit of scripts needs a new build and tag. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-tpub-1 is a PLACEHOLDER the driver may substitute.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-tpub-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-strace-tpub
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_v164order,concurrent4_steady,replay_concurrent4
